Mosquitoes are the vectors of dozens of fatal infectious diseases such as malaria, dengue fever, Zika, encephalitis and yellow fever.

According to the World Health Organization, the number of people who die from mosquito-borne diseases each year is as high as hundreds of thousands, far exceeding that of any other insect.

Mosquitoes are the most lethal pests.

